{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"09e1453b7d9c03fb369519c9ed9b84ac8782471ba3794101fe513577ed75cf51","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_c3e005b4721e7adc338092a1d3555958f23ec5f46f614c4af2c6554408f96c90","overall_assessment":"The paper is technically sound but has significant policy compliance issues, primarily due to the violation of double-blind review policies by including author names, affiliations, and emails. Additionally, the lack of a broader impact statement and explicit ethical considerations is a weakness, though the data usage is compliant with standard practices for public datasets.","paper_id":"B1s6xvqlx","paper_identity_sha256":"11932373e47a5a202270da5dadab207820513b3cc7fcdec4c8ea1fac0a525ab9","prompt_identity_sha256":"99c61d75c176212fca60873c629a8b22307e4f11f6b4765686b15391e8028c2b","raw_response_sha256":"0edea876b85cc08e4ceaf0b13075bf269b05b3c5ebab05658efed9a9891d4683","request_identity_sha256":"32021572d537128f4e36d7c1c9afd223773296b21e2b61927589ef55e7a2a54a","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated section on ethics, fairness, or potential harms. While the work focuses on environment simulation for reinforcement learning, which is generally low-risk, the lack of discussion on dual-use scenarios (e.g., simulating environments for adversarial agents) or broader societal impacts is a minor omission. The authors do discuss limitations regarding model accuracy and generalization, which indirectly addresses reliability concerns, but explicit ethical considerations are absent.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-030","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes standard public datasets: the Arcade Learning Environment (Atari games), TORCS (a racing simulator), and randomly generated 3D mazes. These datasets are widely used in the research community and do not contain personally identifiable information (PII) or sensitive personal data. The use of human-play data for evaluation (e.g., Pong, Breakout, TORCS) is described as interactive testing, but no specific consent forms or privacy protocols are detailed. However, given the nature of the data (game inputs/outputs), privacy risks are minimal. Licensing terms for the datasets are not explicitly cited, but they are standard open-source or academic benchmarks.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors' names (Silvia Chiappa, Sébastien Racaniere, Daan Wierstra & Shakir Mohamed) and their affiliation (DeepMind, London) on the title page. It also provides email addresses ({csilvia, sracaniere, wierstra, shakir}@google.com). This violates double-blind review policies, as the submission clearly identifies the authors and their institution. The acknowledgments section also names specific individuals (David Barber, Alex Pritzel, etc.), further compromising anonymity.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-004","SRC-006","SRC-029"],"review_text":"The paper cites relevant prior work, including Oh et al. (2015) for the baseline comparison and other related works in the introduction. There is no evidence of plagiarism or dual submission in the provided text. The content appears original, with proper attribution to existing methods and datasets. The comparison with Oh et al. (2015) is conducted fairly, with clear distinctions made between the proposed method and the baseline.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement or a checklist for responsible AI practices. While the work is primarily technical, the absence of a discussion on the societal implications of advanced environment simulators (e.g., potential for misuse in creating deceptive simulations) is a gap. The authors do discuss limitations and future work, which is positive, but a more explicit statement on the responsible use of the technology would be beneficial. No IRB or ethics approval is mentioned, which is appropriate given the lack of human subjects in the core experiments (human play is used for evaluation, not as a subject of study).","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"5eaa2f37093eabcf23c9b1d523413075e153ab4a0ab8317c3116fdfc6ae30289","paper_id":"B1s6xvqlx","paper_ordinal":16,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"0edea876b85cc08e4ceaf0b13075bf269b05b3c5ebab05658efed9a9891d4683","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1s6xvqlx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"953afebdc21ac8af1cf1bdeb5f74c8ba9a3a060f266dc9a533aece2e06363dd3","request_identity_sha256":"32021572d537128f4e36d7c1c9afd223773296b21e2b61927589ef55e7a2a54a","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":931,"prompt_tokens":18689,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19620},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"32021572d537128f4e36d7c1c9afd223773296b21e2b61927589ef55e7a2a54a","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}